"Contained popups": what a webview's CEF-owned popups may do, and no bridge in them.

Applies to: tauri-runtime-cef 3.0.0-alpha.7 (crates.io) + 0001, applied in vendor/tauri-runtime-cef.
Not offered upstream yet; `WebviewBuilderCefExt::contain_popups` is the shape it would take.

Why: Eos lets exactly one view open popups, the claude.ai sign-in window, for Google's
sign-in popup (which needs `window.opener`, so it must stay CEF's own popup). Upstream, a
popup inherits its opener's navigation and new-window handlers, which are closures over a
URL alone: they cannot tell the popup from the view, so the popup could go wherever the
view may and open further windows. With `contain_popups(f)` the view's popups decide their
main-frame navigations with `f` instead and every window they ask for is denied. The view's
own handlers are unchanged.

And: CEF hands a popup's renderer only the `extra_info` set in `OnBeforePopup` (none by
default), so the renderer would install `window.ipc` in a popup of a no-bridge view (0001).
A popup of such a view now gets the `tauri:no-bridge` entry, which both render-process
handlers (0001, 0002) already read.

